  "headline": "Nasdaq-100 in a weekend halt near record territory; low tail, high stress on Hormuz crude and climbing global yields",
  "body": "No live Nasdaq-100 price path exists at this timestamp. CME equity index futures are inside the weekend halt and are scheduled to restart near 22:00 UTC, so the assessment is built from the last completed cash session, verified cross-asset levels and the current geopolitical and macro backdrop rather than from observed intraday structure.\n\nThe Nasdaq-100 cash index closed Friday 14 August at 30,046.14, down 0.13% on the session, inside a 29,934.66-30,179.82 range and about 2.3% below the 30,762.20 52-week high, still finishing the week higher. VIX ended at 14.25 (-2.60%), consistent with subdued implied volatility rather than a stressed tape. Treasury constant-maturity yields stood at 4.15% for the 2Y, 4.63% for the 10Y and 5.21% for the 30Y at the latest H.15 publication, against a broader theme of rising long rates globally. The July policy rate was held at 3.50-3.75% for a fifth consecutive meeting.\n\nLatest-session internals were conflicting rather than directional and are treated as stress and confidence inputs, not tail evidence. Technology fell 0.46% as a sector, semiconductor equipment fell 1.71% and application software 1.70%, while the megacap set closed two higher and six lower with Broadcom down about 5.9%; within semiconductors AMD rose 6.5% and Micron 2.3%. That dispersion reduces directional conviction instead of establishing persistent one-way structure.\n\nThe dominant unresolved channel remains energy and geopolitics. The Strait of Hormuz stays effectively disrupted with the U.S. naval blockade in place, Iran-Oman navigation talks stalled, and repeated projectile strikes on Gulf tankers reported through the past week, including three attacks on ADNOC vessels within 48 hours. WTI settled near $82.40 (+1.42%) and Brent near $88.52 (+1.67%), a sixth consecutive daily advance and roughly +5% on the week. This is a live discontinuity source capable of producing a repricing gap at the restart, which is why stress is scored in the high band even with VIX at 14.\n\nNo observed amplifier stack is present: there is no measurable retracement behaviour, no session extremes to hold and no opening structure to score while the market is closed. Under the fixed mapping the current tail of 15 keeps the state green with EA_ON. The week ahead is macro-light into midweek, with FOMC minutes on 19 August the first high-impact scheduled catalyst and flash PMIs on 21 August the second.",
